 - Every assignment is SMART — above all specific and actionable. A fresh / non-inherited handoff (`fork=false`) states its task and acceptance criteria (AC) and carries the full compact contract the child cannot otherwise know: a narrow packet with objective, scope/exclusions, authoritative inputs, acceptance/proof, owners, outputs, interfaces/dependencies, authority/user gates, stop conditions, finite resource limits and an observable status/completion path. An inherited-context handoff (`fork=true`) already carries the task and AC in context, so it designates only the role — you are the sub agent; do this work — and proceeds. Supply essential session input only for the core's inheritance exception; prose grants neither tools nor recursion.
 - Before implementation, the worker inspects task-relevant target/Git state and instructions/records, captures a scoped baseline when attribution matters, and records its contract. Resolve routine gaps with evidence and reversible choices. Record unmet criteria/dependencies rather than silently reducing acceptance.
 - Keep cohesive outcomes as leaves, not artificial editing/testing/reporting children. Split siblings at one abstraction layer, each with inputs, outputs, acceptance/proof, owner, interfaces, dependencies and exclusions; map complete parent coverage and assign a worker integration owner. Unequal size is fine; a parent goal beside its substep is not. Parallel writers need disjoint ownership and isolated branches/worktrees; establish interfaces/order before writing and check the combined result against the baseline.
+- Size each agent's mental space to its task (the `AGENTS.md` focus boundary): default every agent — main and sub alike — to the main agent's own reasoning budget, normally the session default, and raise it only for genuinely complex work or an agent that repeatedly fails. This is about focus, not only cost — prefer a separate handoff over loading unrelated tasks into one agent, and avoid needless long reasoning, because a bloated or multi-purpose context degrades focus.
 - On context pressure or resource exhaustion, checkpoint artifacts, revision, decisions, remaining acceptance and next actions. Split independent remainders with coverage/interfaces or route an unsplittable remainder to a fresh replacement under unchanged authority/acceptance. When attempts yield no useful evidence, change the hypothesis/check or route a bounded permitted specialist task; stop repetitive avenues and report incomplete, not an endless loop.
 - Use the project's work-record convention; absent one, use `.scratch/active-work.md` as an entry point. Preserve other entries in the ticket/work-record ledger only — tickets are append-style, fact documents are not. Keep unfinished work discoverable: objective/scope/acceptance, owner/status, input/output paths, authority/gates/user availability, decisions, baseline/current revision and dirt, checks/review and covered revision, blockers/next action, and any running-job result/continuation. After a status signal, continue the next authorized step. Remove only this task's active link after independent acceptance and any user gate. On resumption compare records with current target/Git state and rerun stale checks, not session memory.
 
 ## Proof and review
 
 - Implement only authorized behavior. Reproduce defects where practical and use checks capable of detecting them. Run target-project gates and risk-driven checks, inspect the scoped final diff, and run scoped `git diff --check` for text. Identify unexercised criteria when a runner, hardware or external system is unavailable; separate existing failures from introduced ones.
-- Bind evidence to commit or working-tree hashes, commands/results and inspectable artifacts; rerun invalidated checks. Integration proves the combined outcome/interfaces, not child verdicts. Self-tests and unrun tests are not independent acceptance.
+- Bind evidence to commit or working-tree hashes, commands/results and inspectable artifacts; rerun invalidated checks. Integration proves the combined outcome/interfaces, not child verdicts. A self-test is the in-slice loop, not independent acceptance; unrun tests are not evidence.
+- The slice gate reviews the accumulated slice outcome — the bounded end-to-end user outcome defined under Product decisions — not the individual tasks inside it, and runs wherever in the slice that outcome is reviewable.
 - Give a fresh reviewer the objective, full acceptance, final scoped revision/artifacts, evidence, constraints and repair authority/tools. The reviewer attempts to falsify acceptance through missing scope, safety, regressions and stale proof. Record material defects with location, violated criterion and reproduction/evidence. Repair only within authority/tools; otherwise label and route an assigned-writer fallback. After repair and renewed self-tests, route another fresh reviewer; never accept the repairer's own verdict.
 - Review material defects, not speculative polish. PASS covers full acceptance at the reviewed revision; unknown acceptance is not PASS. Unavailable independent review is an infrastructure blocker, not self-review permission. At finite review/no-progress limits, save unresolved criteria and the next useful action, disclose non-blocking limits and report incomplete where acceptance remains unmet.
 
 ## Product decisions
 
 - Main resolves consequential kickoff uncertainty using confirmed goals/principles/preferences. Present concrete alternatives, effects and a recommendation, not implementation trivia. Workers research implementation choices. A choice is consequential when it changes user workflows/capabilities, requirements/acceptance, recurring cost/duties, dependencies, data handling, migration burden or promised scope; apply confirmed project thresholds. For authorized consequential choices, workers record source, affected behavior, trade-off, validation/revisit condition. An `approved` label alone is not provenance; principles do not grant operational authority.
-- When product uncertainty warrants slices, main defines bounded end-to-end user outcomes and delegates concrete review artifacts: runnable demo, HTML, screens, recording or readable actual evidence suited to the task. A POC states hypothesis, proof method and continuation criterion upfront. Deliver the actual artifact at an agreed user gate and pause dependent work until approval or explicit waiver. Do not invent mandatory stages/gates for tiny clear tasks.
+- When product uncertainty warrants slices, main defines bounded end-to-end user outcomes — each such outcome is a vertical slice — and delegates concrete review artifacts: runnable demo, HTML, screens, recording or readable actual evidence suited to the task. A POC states hypothesis, proof method and continuation criterion upfront. Deliver the actual artifact at an agreed user gate and pause dependent work until approval or explicit waiver. Do not invent mandatory stages/gates for tiny clear tasks.
 - On feedback, respect user-owned goals/preferences and verify factual claims, diagnoses and proposed fixes. Correct results through workers, trace originating assumptions/decisions, and update the highest necessary confirmed requirements/principles and affected downstream work. Explain constraint conflicts and mark unresolved interpretations provisional; do not infer personality or rewrite unrelated principles.
 - Main delivers a concise user-visible conclusion through confirmed goals/scenarios, evidence, limits and genuinely needed action, not internal discussion. Distinguish reviewer-backed results, incomplete work and untested behavior; plans are not results.
 
